# WP-LWC (11-25): Large World Coordinates witness - the same set at the origin and at X = 2,000,000 cm (20 km).
# Pass 1 (baseline): world positions are float today (TransformComponent.hpp:30 glm::vec3); 1 unit = 1 cm, so at 20 km
# a float step is 0.125 cm and the view/shadow/TAA maths cancels two ~2e6 numbers. The origin set must be still
# between frames; the 20 km set records today's defect per catalogue row (L-A01 vertex jitter, L-A02 shadow swim,
# L-A03 TAA smear). The pose is frozen (CesiumMan PlaybackSpeed 0): a still camera + a still pose must give
# identical frames - any difference between N and N+1 is precision, not animation. Catalogue: scratch/WP-LWC/CATALOGUE.md.
